  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Founded in 1983, the Cercle Canin de Grasse (CC06) is a non-profit association affiliated to the Société canine régionale Midi Côte d'Azur, run by volunteer instructors qualified by the Société centrale canine. Its main aim remains family training for dogs and puppies; agility, hoopers and obedience complete the offer. Tracking is presented as a closed section, and workshops are organised on request (agility, hoopers, obedience, tracking, cooperative care, clicker).</p>

      <h2>The ground</h2>
      <p>The club occupies the former Roquevignon quarry, developed by its founders: marked-out grounds, toilets, water and electricity, club rooms. The site is provided by the town of Grasse. On the main ground, synthetic turf has replaced the gravel; a fenced, marked-out area is reserved for the puppy school, created in 2003.</p>

      <h2>The classes</h2>
      <p>Dog training classes take place every Wednesday and Saturday, in groups and by level: static commands (sit, down, stand, stay), recall, walking on and off the lead, leave it, socialisation and instructors' advice. The puppy school is for dogs aged 2 to 5 months; the club asks you to bring a lead, flat collar or harness, treats and toys. Agility is open to all dogs (categories S, under 35 cm; M, 35 to under 43 cm; I, 43 to under 48 cm; L, 48 cm and over, with a handi class). Hoopers, with no jumping, suit dogs of all sizes and ages. Obedience requires a dog that is sociable with other dogs and with people, with a minimum of recall and motivation for food or toys; competitions start at 12 months.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The official website (cc06.net) gives the address chemin de Roquevignon, 06130 Grasse, the phone number 04 93 36 50 42 and the email cerclecanindegrasse@gmail.com. For a first visit, the club's FAQ asks you to phone: the club tells you the next sessions of the chosen activity and whether places remain, and the first class is free. The 2026-2027 schedule and the start-of-year prices are published on the "Tarifs et horaires" page as images, with a registration form. The site noted that there would be no class on Saturday 19 September (agility competition).</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before coming to book the free first session, and bring a lead, treats and toys.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The historic centre of Grasse, the world capital of perfume, is easy to visit from the club.</p>
